  "nl_text": "The schemabench_0110 database contains 12 tables, each with its own unique purpose. The first table, \"awards,\" stores information about individual awards, including the title, effective and expiration dates, amount, instrument, organization code, program officer, abstract narration, minimum and maximum AMD letter dates, ARRA amount, and award ID. The award ID is the primary key, and the organization code is a foreign key that references the organization table. The foa_info table contains information about the funding agency, including the code and name. The foa_info_awards table links the award ID and the funding agency code, allowing for the assignment of multiple funding agencies to a single award. The institution table contains information about the institution that received the award, including the name, city, zip code, contact, address, country, state, and state code. The institution_awards table links the award ID and the institution name and zip code, allowing for the assignment of multiple institutions to a single award. The investigator table contains information about the investigator, including the email ID, first name, and last name. The investigator_awards table links the award ID and the investigator email ID, allowing for the assignment of multiple investigators to a single award. The organization table contains information about the organization, including the code and division. The program_element table contains information about the program element, including the code and text. The program_element_awards table links the award ID and the program element code, allowing for the assignment of multiple program elements to a single award. The program_reference table contains information about the program reference, including the code and text. The program_reference_awards table links the award ID and the program reference code, allowing for the assignment of multiple program references to a single award.",
  "gold_question": "1) Background / Context\nThe project involves working with a dataset of funding grants provided by the National Science Foundation (NSF). The primary focus is to analyze this data to predict the award amounts for research grants, thereby assisting in decision-making processes.\n\n 2) Objectives\n- Develop a system that predicts award amounts for NSF grants.\n- Use historical grant data to aid in accurate forecasting.\n- Facilitate data analysis to improve grant management and decision-making.\n\n 3) Stakeholders & Users\n- Primary Users: Data analysts, NSF grant officers, research institutions.\n- Stakeholders: National Science Foundation, research applicants, policy makers.\n\n 4) Functional Descriptions\n- Data Management: Ingest and manage grant data, including details about awards, investigators, institutions, and program elements.\n- Prediction Engine: Develop algorithms to predict award amounts based on historical data.\n- Reporting: Generate detailed reports for insights into award distribution and trends.\n- User Interface: Provide a UI for users to input data queries and view prediction outcomes.\n\n 5) Non-Functional Descriptions\n- Performance: The system should handle large volumes of data with efficient querying capabilities.\n- Scalability: Handle increases in data size without loss of performance as more historical data becomes available.\n- Security: Ensure data privacy and secure access to sensitive grant and applicant information.\n- Usability: User interfaces must be intuitive and accessible for users with varying levels of expertise in data analysis.",
  "input_json": "/data/SchemaBench/Experiment/schema2text_codellama13b/0110.json",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: schemabench_0110\nCREATE TABLE `awards` (\n  `award_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `title` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `effective_date` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `expiration_date` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `amount` decimal(10,2) NOT NULL,\n  `instrument` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `organization_code` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  `program_officer` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `abstract_narration` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  `min_amd_letter_date` date DEFAULT NULL,\n  `max_amd_letter_date` date DEFAULT NULL,\n  `arra_amount` decimal(10,2) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`award_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `awards_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`organization_code`) REFERENCES `organization` (`code`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `foa_info` (\n  `code` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`code`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `foa_info_awards` (\n  `award_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `funding_agency_code` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`award_id`, `funding_agency_code`),\n  CONSTRAINT `foa_info_awards_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`award_id`) REFERENCES `awards` (`award_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `foa_info_awards_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`funding_agency_code`) REFERENCES `foa_info` (`code`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `institution` (\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `city` varchar(100) NOT NULL,\n  `zip_code` varchar(20) NOT NULL,\n  `contact` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `address` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `country` varchar(100) NOT NULL,\n  `state` varchar(100) NOT NULL,\n  `state_code` varchar(10) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`name`, `zip_code`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `institution_awards` (\n  `award_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `institution_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `institution_zip_code` varchar(20) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`award_id`, `institution_name`, `institution_zip_code`),\n  CONSTRAINT `institution_awards_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`award_id`) REFERENCES `awards` (`award_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `institution_awards_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`institution_name`, `institution_zip_code`) REFERENCES `institution` (`name`, `zip_code`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `investigator` (\n  `email_id` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `first_name` varchar(100) NOT NULL,\n  `last_name` varchar(100) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`email_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `investigator_awards` (\n  `award_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `investigator_email_id` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`award_id`, `investigator_email_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `investigator_awards_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`award_id`) REFERENCES `awards` (`award_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `investigator_awards_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`investigator_email_id`) REFERENCES `investigator` (`email_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `organization` (\n  `code` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  `division` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`code`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `program_element` (\n  `code` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  `text` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`code`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `program_element_awards` (\n  `award_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `program_element_code` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`award_id`, `program_element_code`),\n  CONSTRAINT `program_element_awards_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`award_id`) REFERENCES `awards` (`award_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `program_element_awards_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`program_element_code`) REFERENCES `program_element` (`code`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `program_reference` (\n  `code` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  `text` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`code`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `program_reference_awards` (\n  `award_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `program_reference_code` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`award_id`, `program_reference_code`),\n  CONSTRAINT `program_reference_awards_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`award_id`) REFERENCES `awards` (`award_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `program_reference_awards_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`program_reference_code`) REFERENCES `program_reference` (`code`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
